ROCKNIX/kodi-app: Kodi runs as root inside the ES session - logind block
inhibitors cannot stop its power menu (live incident 2026-07-19: accidental
full poweroff from Kodi). Powerdown / Reboot / Hibernate report unavailable
so Kodi hides them: quitting is the only way out of the app, and Suspend
stays NATIVE (the session survives sleep, Steam-like resume - the user's
chosen semantics).

--- a/xbmc/platform/linux/powermanagement/LogindUPowerSyscall.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/platform/linux/powermanagement/LogindUPowerSyscall.cpp
@@ -100,21 +100,21 @@
 bool CLogindUPowerSyscall::CanPowerdown()
 {
-  return m_canPowerdown;
+  return false; // ROCKNIX: hidden - quitting Kodi is the only way out
 }
 
 bool CLogindUPowerSyscall::CanSuspend()
 {
   return m_canSuspend;
 }
 
 bool CLogindUPowerSyscall::CanHibernate()
 {
-  return m_canHibernate;
+  return false; // ROCKNIX: hidden
 }
 
 bool CLogindUPowerSyscall::CanReboot()
 {
-  return m_canReboot;
+  return false; // ROCKNIX: hidden
 }
 
 bool CLogindUPowerSyscall::HasLogind()
